  "title": "Haze4K Observable Signal Calibration Decomposition v1",
  "rationale": "Decompose the archived all-keep failure without reopening its closed contextual-head family or changing the model, representation, data roles, action scales, utility margin, risk limit, or precision target. One shared predictor is evaluated as P00 raw utility plus raw risk, P10 utility-corrected only, P01 risk-corrected only, and P11 fully corrected. The same 600 original-clear-scene OOF population supplies the primary five-endpoint Bonferroni family; 150 scenes remain calibration-only nuisance data; and the already exposed 100-scene test-development role remains secondary stress evidence with four variants nested within scene. GT is a privileged positive control only, while deterministic prediction-target permutation, keep identity, uniform, and action-map shuffle are negative or matched controls. Cloud retains checkpoints, raw predictions, targets, action maps, and SHA inventories; GitHub receives only compact scene-grouped and aggregate evidence.",
  "first_operation": "HAZE4K_OBSERVABLE_SIGNAL_CALIBRATION_DECOMPOSE",
